WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.546
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:11.816 --> 00:15.186
How much money does it take to live alone?

3
00:16.888 --> 00:20.091
Can I live alone on that money?

4
00:21.259 --> 00:23.394
All of her life insurance money

5
00:25.096 --> 00:28.500
is proof of her love.

6
00:33.371 --> 00:38.076
Okay, I got it. I'm now your personal advisor.

7
00:39.878 --> 00:43.815
The mountain guide Motoka Tabatake's life insurance is 30 million yen.

8
00:44.516 --> 00:49.921
If the cause of death is suicide, it isn't paid.

9
00:52.824 --> 00:55.493
I didn't do it.

10
00:56.227 --> 00:57.495
I didn't.

11
00:57.562 --> 00:59.764
Do you think Saruwatari really did it?

12
01:00.965 --> 01:03.902
As long as there's evidence, we'll consider her a suspect.

13
01:04.469 --> 01:06.037
It's Ogoma.

14
01:06.104 --> 01:07.972
Don't admit to what you didn't do.

15
01:09.174 --> 01:15.613
If the three missing people were alive, we would know who is telling the truth.

16
01:16.748 --> 01:17.916
It's Mr. Monden, right?

17
01:17.982 --> 01:21.085
He's supposed to be missing, so why is he in Shibuya?

18
01:21.152 --> 01:22.420
He's alive.

19
01:24.789 --> 01:26.124
He's a witness.

20
01:28.293 --> 01:30.361
Doubt everything.

21
01:30.428 --> 01:34.799
Once you have doubted everything, what remains is the truth.

22
01:37.735 --> 01:40.138
-He's really the missing Mr. Monden? -Good morning.

23
01:40.205 --> 01:41.606
Thank you, and yes.

24
01:41.673 --> 01:44.409
Huh? If he's safe, why doesn't he come forward?

25
01:44.475 --> 01:45.310
Mr. Nao.

26
01:45.376 --> 01:47.312
Rescue teams are searching the mountain, right?

27
01:47.378 --> 01:48.880
Yes, desperately.

28
01:48.947 --> 01:50.381
What does he do for work?

29
01:50.448 --> 01:52.317
He's an office worker in Sapporo.

30
01:52.383 --> 01:53.985
And he came to Tokyo?

31
01:54.485 --> 01:56.921
He's pretending to be missing?

32
01:57.689 --> 01:59.524
He doesn't try to go inside.

33
01:59.591 --> 02:04.429
He wasn't invited, and he may not have a key to the room.

34
02:04.495 --> 02:07.398
I'll secure Mr. Monden and get his side of the story.

35
02:07.465 --> 02:09.667
What? You plan to look for this man?

36
02:09.734 --> 02:13.504
Yes. I'll make him tell me what happened on the mountain.

37
02:13.571 --> 02:14.539
No…

38
02:15.240 --> 02:18.042
Who gave Mr. Nikaido the sleeping pill?

39
02:20.111 --> 02:22.213
What is his relationship with Harune?

40
02:22.280 --> 02:25.450
Are you sure? He's not a serial killer, is he?

41
02:26.384 --> 02:30.021
Could the other two missing people have been killed on the mountain?

42
02:30.088 --> 02:31.723
One of them is Mr. Monden's wife.

43
02:33.591 --> 02:35.260
Husbands, wives, parents, children.

44
02:35.326 --> 02:36.794
They kill each other all the time.

45
02:37.762 --> 02:39.497
Generally, they don't.

46
02:40.365 --> 02:41.966
I'll borrow the residential map.

47
02:49.674 --> 02:50.375
It's hot!

48
02:51.276 --> 02:55.046
I think the camera was around here.

49
02:56.781 --> 02:59.350
-Why is even the shade hot? -It's summer.

50
02:59.417 --> 03:01.352
So hot! What is that?

51
03:02.020 --> 03:03.855
It looks like it's here.

52
03:03.921 --> 03:06.190
-Right? -Yes. All right.

53
03:06.257 --> 03:08.126
-Be careful. -Yes.

54
03:08.192 --> 03:10.295
So he's alive…

55
03:11.929 --> 03:13.531
Coming!

56
03:13.598 --> 03:15.867
-Excuse me, may I speak with you? -Hello.

57
03:15.933 --> 03:17.135
Sure. What is it?

58
03:17.201 --> 03:20.405
Have you seen the person in this photo?

59
03:21.873 --> 03:23.107
No, I haven't.

60
03:23.174 --> 03:24.108
No?

61
03:24.175 --> 03:28.012
I only work three days a week. And not at night.

62
03:28.079 --> 03:30.682
Do you know the man in apartment 206?

63
03:30.748 --> 03:33.284
The one next to the stairs? Mr. Nikaido?

64
03:33.351 --> 03:34.485
Yes!

65
03:34.552 --> 03:37.889
He's from Hokkaido, right? He once gave me butter candy.

66
03:37.955 --> 03:38.756
NIKAIDO

67
03:38.823 --> 03:41.359
When did you last see him?

68
03:41.426 --> 03:43.361
About a month ago?

69
03:43.428 --> 03:46.431
He uses the place when he has work in Tokyo.

70
03:46.497 --> 03:49.067
What kind of work in Tokyo?

71
03:49.133 --> 03:51.803
He runs a restaurant, right? It must be related to that.

72
03:51.869 --> 03:54.205
May I check the security camera footage?

73
03:54.272 --> 03:56.140
It's just a fake, you know.

74
03:59.043 --> 04:01.479
If you remember anything…

75
04:02.080 --> 04:03.781
-Wait a moment. -Yes.

76
04:03.848 --> 04:04.849
Yes?

77
04:10.121 --> 04:12.690
-What are you even doing? -Oh, sorry!

78
04:12.757 --> 04:14.992
That was an accident. Is there anything?

79
04:15.059 --> 04:17.862
Seriously? Nothing but flyers?

80
04:17.929 --> 04:19.630
Is there nothing worthwhile?

81
04:19.697 --> 04:20.631
NIKAIDO

82
04:20.698 --> 04:23.067
Look, there's something.

83
04:23.634 --> 04:24.736
What is this?

84
04:27.739 --> 04:29.307
Excuse me.

85
04:29.374 --> 04:30.975
Sorry, we're not open for lunch yet.

86
04:31.042 --> 04:35.012
May I speak with you? About the people in this photo?

87
04:35.780 --> 04:38.015
I haven't seen either of them.

88
04:39.417 --> 04:44.188
This man appeared on your security camera around 9:00 p.m. two nights ago.

89
04:44.922 --> 04:46.524
What are you investigating?

90
04:47.024 --> 04:50.828
Insurance investigation. There was a car accident near here.

91
04:50.895 --> 04:52.363
A car accident?

92
04:52.430 --> 04:53.765
Was there?

93
04:53.831 --> 04:56.134
-There was! -No, there…

94
04:56.200 --> 04:58.569
I don't know, so please try asking someone else.

95
05:02.707 --> 05:04.275
What is this?

96
05:04.842 --> 05:06.511
11 digits…

97
05:07.412 --> 05:09.447
A product serial number?

98
05:09.514 --> 05:10.915
Overseas bank code?

99
05:10.982 --> 05:13.351
But it wouldn't be lined up like this.

100
05:13.418 --> 05:15.086
Isn't it just a password?

101
05:15.153 --> 05:16.187
For what?

102
05:16.254 --> 05:17.255
Wi-Fi.

103
05:17.321 --> 05:18.923
Why stick it there?

104
05:19.424 --> 05:20.625
You wouldn't, would you?

105
05:21.459 --> 05:23.561
Let's look into this too.

106
05:23.628 --> 05:25.496
What are you going to do now?

107
05:25.563 --> 05:28.766
Go door to door. Detectives do the legwork.

108
05:30.635 --> 05:31.869
That's cool.

109
05:31.936 --> 05:34.605
-Are you mocking me? -I'm not.

110
05:35.473 --> 05:37.041
Will you work with the police?

111
05:37.108 --> 05:38.576
No way.

112
05:39.477 --> 05:42.447
If I ask anything, they'll report back to Hokkaido.

113
05:42.513 --> 05:45.149
And everything I'm doing will be reported too.

114
05:46.584 --> 05:49.353
So we'll investigate and not tell the police?

115
05:50.021 --> 05:52.723
I don't know how much or what they are covering up.

116
05:53.591 --> 05:55.126
You know what I always say.

117
05:55.993 --> 05:57.028
Doubt everything?

118
05:57.528 --> 05:58.963
Tokyo is big, you know?

119
05:59.030 --> 06:00.131
I know.

120
06:00.198 --> 06:01.933
Then I'll go

121
06:01.999 --> 06:06.404
check out the CCTV cameras and ask if they can give us footage.

122
06:11.576 --> 06:12.677
All done!

123
06:17.648 --> 06:18.816
Let's go then.

124
06:19.517 --> 06:20.351
Let's do it!

125
06:38.436 --> 06:40.805
Let me confirm again.

126
06:42.173 --> 06:46.577
Only your fingerprints and Mr. Nikaido's were found on the bottle.

127
06:47.678 --> 06:51.916
I'm only telling you what I saw.

128
06:51.983 --> 06:55.820
The place where you got lost is on a route no longer used for hiking.

129
06:56.821 --> 06:58.089
Where were you going?

130
06:58.155 --> 06:59.790
That's because…

131
07:02.827 --> 07:04.929
I've told you so many times.

132
07:05.763 --> 07:07.899
Excuse me! Do you have a moment?

133
07:07.965 --> 07:08.966
Huh? Police?

134
07:09.033 --> 07:10.902
No. I'm looking for people…

135
07:10.968 --> 07:12.236
It's okay.

136
07:13.337 --> 07:14.739
I'm here.

137
07:14.805 --> 07:17.441
-If you see them-- -Okay, got it.

138
07:18.042 --> 07:19.877
Have you seen them anywhere?

139
07:19.944 --> 07:21.612
No, I haven't.

140
07:21.679 --> 07:22.847
I don't know.

141
07:23.614 --> 07:24.448
Come on.

142
07:26.417 --> 07:28.653
You won't turn into scum.

143
07:29.453 --> 07:31.956
May I look at the security camera footage?

144
07:32.023 --> 07:33.257
Who are you?

145
07:33.324 --> 07:34.926
I'm looking for some people.

146
07:34.992 --> 07:36.460
We can't show it to civilians.

147
07:37.028 --> 07:39.363
-Are you police? -No, I'm not.

148
07:39.430 --> 07:40.965
Which area are you looking in?

149
07:41.032 --> 07:42.600
Hold on.

150
07:42.667 --> 07:43.801
-May I use your map? -Yes.

151
07:43.868 --> 07:44.869
Here.

152
07:44.936 --> 07:45.836
Come on!

153
07:45.903 --> 07:47.572
-That's too wide! -Impossible!

154
07:47.638 --> 07:49.640
You'll need a car to search all of this!

155
07:49.707 --> 07:51.075
I don't have a car.

156
07:51.142 --> 07:52.276
A bicycle?

157
07:52.343 --> 07:53.277
Get a rental one!

158
07:53.344 --> 07:56.414
Go ahead! Go on through!

159
07:56.480 --> 08:01.052
Excuse me. If you see them, please call this number.

160
08:01.118 --> 08:03.187
-Wait. Show me again. -Yes?

161
08:06.057 --> 08:09.527
Would she really throw away 30 million yen that she could give her daughter?

162
08:09.594 --> 08:10.528
I love you.

163
08:10.595 --> 08:12.597
PAID PARKING

164
08:12.663 --> 08:15.866
Hello. I'm Nao of Zennichi Insurance Research.

165
08:15.933 --> 08:19.370
I'm looking for a hit-and-run vehicle.

166
08:19.437 --> 08:20.871
Welcome, you can sit anywhere.

167
08:20.938 --> 08:22.440
-Excuse me. -Yes?

168
08:22.506 --> 08:25.509
Are those your shop's security cameras?

169
08:27.478 --> 08:30.448
In Hokkaido, I could cover the whole town in half a day.

170
08:30.948 --> 08:33.651
-Will you go back to Hokkaido, then? -Who said I would go back?

171
08:33.718 --> 08:37.021
I took leave to come to Tokyo, so I'm not going back empty-handed.

172
08:37.088 --> 08:38.623
Did you find anything?

173
08:38.689 --> 08:40.491
No. But I'm just getting started.

174
08:40.558 --> 08:42.226
So you found nothing.

175
08:42.293 --> 08:44.562
Tomorrow, I'll widen the search area.

176
08:47.164 --> 08:50.468
Mr. Monden lives in Sapporo, right?

177
08:51.569 --> 08:53.771
He may be staying somewhere.

178
08:56.307 --> 08:57.541
Where are you staying?

179
08:57.608 --> 08:59.777
What? Me?

180
09:00.478 --> 09:02.013
The place I always stay.

181
09:04.115 --> 09:05.716
Does your place have room?

182
09:08.786 --> 09:10.655
Haven't you booked a hotel?

183
09:10.721 --> 09:14.625
It's summer vacation. All the cheap places are full.

184
09:14.692 --> 09:18.629
The only available ones cost as much as rent. Around 30,000 yen a night.

185
09:24.635 --> 09:28.172
I'll try negotiating to see if you can stay.

186
09:28.239 --> 09:29.640
Want to come with me?

187
09:29.707 --> 09:31.175
NAO

188
09:31.242 --> 09:32.076
-Hup. -What?

189
09:33.310 --> 09:35.579
Is this your home?

190
09:35.646 --> 09:36.547
Yes.

191
09:37.114 --> 09:38.816
Don't you work in Hokkaido?

192
09:38.883 --> 09:40.518
I worked in Tokyo until two years ago.

193
09:41.085 --> 09:43.087
I hope they haven't changed the lock.

194
09:43.154 --> 09:45.589
All right, it opened. Come in.

195
09:45.656 --> 09:46.924
Excuse me.

196
09:50.561 --> 09:52.697
-Who are you? -Oh, I'm sorry…

197
09:52.763 --> 09:54.265
I'm no one suspicious.

198
09:54.331 --> 09:56.801
I'm home! Go on in.

199
09:57.368 --> 09:59.603
Are you sure I can stay?

200
09:59.670 --> 10:00.538
Probably.

201
10:00.604 --> 10:01.639
Probably?

202
10:01.706 --> 10:03.374
Did you eat dinner? I bought food.

203
10:03.441 --> 10:04.475
-Hey! -What?

204
10:04.542 --> 10:07.211
Won't I be bothering her? Who is that?

205
10:07.278 --> 10:08.312
My wife.

206
10:09.747 --> 10:10.915
Akane.

207
10:11.882 --> 10:13.284
You're married?

208
10:13.350 --> 10:15.052
Is that so surprising?

209
10:19.323 --> 10:20.491
Excuse me.

210
10:21.659 --> 10:23.227
The food will be ready soon.

211
10:23.294 --> 10:25.996
A detective from Hokkaido you met at work?

212
10:26.063 --> 10:27.298
Yes.

213
10:28.332 --> 10:31.235
She's very cautious, so show her proof you're trustworthy.

214
10:31.302 --> 10:32.336
Yes.

215
10:36.574 --> 10:39.043
I am Ogoma of the Hokkaido Prefectural Police.

216
10:39.110 --> 10:40.077
Your police badge?

217
10:40.845 --> 10:42.913
They can't carry it around on vacation.

218
10:42.980 --> 10:44.048
Sorry.

219
10:47.284 --> 10:49.320
I bet you're wondering, "Is he the real thing?"

220
10:50.621 --> 10:54.525
People keep asking if I'm impersonating a cop or running a con.

221
10:55.159 --> 10:58.062
People from Tokyo are very cautious.

222
11:02.333 --> 11:04.335
You are on leave, right?

223
11:04.401 --> 11:05.536
Yes.

224
11:05.603 --> 11:07.238
I took time off.

225
11:08.205 --> 11:10.241
And you're still investigating?

226
11:10.808 --> 11:12.843
He's looking for a witness.

227
11:14.311 --> 11:16.147
Is it an official investigation?

228
11:16.814 --> 11:18.549
No, it's an independent one.

229
11:19.116 --> 11:20.384
Independent?

230
11:20.451 --> 11:22.720
Don't press him.

231
11:22.787 --> 11:26.390
He wants to rescue his benefactor from trouble.

232
11:26.457 --> 11:29.994
That's also true, but as police, it's a case I can't ignore.

233
11:31.595 --> 11:33.497
Then why independently investigate?

234
11:33.564 --> 11:34.465
Here you go.

235
11:34.532 --> 11:37.168
You're right to ask that.

236
11:37.234 --> 11:41.272
It's a long story, so let's eat first.

237
11:42.239 --> 11:44.074
Okay? All done.

238
11:45.843 --> 11:47.812
Let's eat.

239
11:47.878 --> 11:49.446
Thanks for the food.

240
11:59.223 --> 12:00.491
So good!

241
12:00.558 --> 12:01.792
It's good.

242
12:03.694 --> 12:07.965
This meat was on sale too. It's good meat, right?

243
12:08.032 --> 12:09.500
It's not bad.

244
12:22.513 --> 12:24.248
-How is it? -Average.

245
12:25.583 --> 12:26.917
Average is best.

246
12:29.186 --> 12:32.323
I guess I'll use this sauce.

247
12:32.389 --> 12:35.726
May I ask how you two met?

248
12:37.728 --> 12:38.896
You really want to know?

249
12:40.664 --> 12:41.599
Sorry.

250
12:48.072 --> 12:49.206
Delicious.

251
12:55.613 --> 12:57.915
Use the house as you like.

252
12:57.982 --> 12:59.850
I have work tomorrow.

253
12:59.917 --> 13:02.086
Thank you for letting me stay.

254
13:02.152 --> 13:03.020
Mr. Nao--

255
13:03.087 --> 13:06.090
We have been separated for two years.

256
13:08.726 --> 13:11.061
You shouldn't trust that man too much.

257
13:27.745 --> 13:28.946
What's wrong?

258
13:31.282 --> 13:34.351
How long has it been since you last saw your wife?

259
13:34.418 --> 13:36.887
Huh? A year and…

260
13:37.821 --> 13:39.290
four months?

261
13:41.592 --> 13:46.764
If you need to speak with Akane, I'll stay at an internet café.

262
13:46.830 --> 13:48.032
Speak to?

263
13:48.098 --> 13:48.966
Yes.

264
13:52.002 --> 13:53.170
Not really.

265
13:55.139 --> 13:56.807
-Really? -Ogoma, are you married?

266
13:56.874 --> 13:59.543
I would like to someday.

267
13:59.610 --> 14:02.479
But no one wants to live in my remote district.

268
14:02.546 --> 14:05.115
Maybe find a girlfriend who loves mountains and nature.

269
14:05.182 --> 14:08.419
I'll just get promoted to a bigger station and get out of there.

270
14:08.485 --> 14:09.920
-Promotion? -Yes.

271
14:10.621 --> 14:12.389
-A positive mindset. -Yes!

272
14:12.456 --> 14:14.792
Tomorrow will be dangerously hot too.

273
14:14.858 --> 14:17.294
-So sleep well. -Yes.

274
14:17.361 --> 14:20.064
-Okay, good night. -Good night.

275
14:31.241 --> 14:32.843
Sorry for worrying you.

276
14:32.910 --> 14:35.946
And thank you for being on my side.

277
15:14.051 --> 15:15.185
Good morning.

278
15:18.088 --> 15:19.456
Where's Ogoma?

279
15:20.157 --> 15:21.592
He already went out.

280
15:24.028 --> 15:26.964
Looking for someone in just five days…

281
15:27.631 --> 15:30.300
It's impossible, but he will try anyway. That's who he is.

282
15:31.035 --> 15:34.204
This is the biggest case of his detective career.

283
15:34.271 --> 15:37.141
It's complicated, but he must solve it.

284
15:42.679 --> 15:44.148
How long will you stay?

285
15:45.983 --> 15:47.518
Could I stay here for a while?

286
15:50.988 --> 15:53.624
I'll sleep over there. I'm grabbing a cup of coffee.

287
16:06.403 --> 16:07.538
Good morning.

288
16:07.604 --> 16:09.540
Sorry for calling you so early.

289
16:09.606 --> 16:11.942
It's okay. What's wrong?

290
16:12.009 --> 16:15.679
It's about my sister's life insurance.

291
16:15.746 --> 16:18.082
-Did you get the death certificate? -Yes.

292
16:18.148 --> 16:21.752
In the "cause of death," which box did they tick?

293
16:23.087 --> 16:24.488
Suicide.

294
16:25.556 --> 16:29.726
If the cause is suicide, the insurance won't pay, right?

295
16:30.327 --> 16:33.197
I would like you to look into something.

296
16:35.365 --> 16:38.202
About my sister's suicide.

297
16:38.268 --> 16:42.573
As a family member, I'm sure you feel that something is off.

298
16:43.307 --> 16:44.475
Yes.

299
16:46.510 --> 16:48.612
If I investigate,

300
16:48.679 --> 16:52.349
I'll need to talk fees and expenses.

301
16:53.350 --> 16:56.153
How much would I need to pay?

302
16:56.720 --> 17:00.991
If I prove your sister's death was not suicide

303
17:01.058 --> 17:03.760
and the insurance is paid,

304
17:03.827 --> 17:06.230
I take ten percent as my fee.

305
17:08.165 --> 17:09.800
Not suicide?

306
17:12.369 --> 17:13.504
How about it?

307
17:14.037 --> 17:16.607
I think it's not a bad deal.

308
17:19.676 --> 17:21.745
Have you seen these people?

309
17:22.579 --> 17:23.580
Take care.

310
17:24.481 --> 17:25.849
Let me check.

311
17:25.916 --> 17:27.317
You can't sit here!

312
17:28.852 --> 17:30.053
Don't you have school?

313
17:30.554 --> 17:31.688
Thank you.

314
17:31.755 --> 17:33.090
Take care.

315
17:37.895 --> 17:41.632
I may have seen them, they have been staying several nights.

316
17:41.698 --> 17:43.767
-Excuse me. I'm opening the door. -Okay.

317
17:45.269 --> 17:46.770
What is it?

318
17:47.571 --> 17:49.273
You don't look similar at all. Sorry.

319
17:49.339 --> 17:52.509
"13@…"

320
17:52.576 --> 17:53.644
Hey.

321
17:53.710 --> 17:55.746
I'm looking for some people.

322
17:55.812 --> 17:57.181
Have you seen them?

323
17:57.247 --> 17:58.549
We don't know.

324
17:58.615 --> 17:59.816
Is this a scam?

325
17:59.883 --> 18:01.885
-It's not! -You're scary.

326
18:01.952 --> 18:03.554
How am I scary?

327
18:04.454 --> 18:06.290
Excuse me. Have you seen these people?

328
18:06.356 --> 18:07.524
-No? -No clue.

329
18:07.591 --> 18:08.258
You don't know?

330
18:08.325 --> 18:08.992
I guess not.

331
18:09.059 --> 18:11.495
Have you seen these people?

332
18:11.562 --> 18:12.729
I haven't.

333
18:12.796 --> 18:14.031
Anyone who looks similar?

334
18:14.097 --> 18:15.032
Hello.

335
18:15.098 --> 18:17.868
Have you seen these people?

336
18:22.439 --> 18:25.209
We close at 8:00 p.m., understood?

337
18:39.523 --> 18:43.460
I'M TAKAHASHI FROM THE CONSTRUCTION SITE I FOUND SOMEONE WHO HAS SEEN THEM!

338
18:43.527 --> 18:45.195
Yes!

339
18:45.262 --> 18:47.197
We close at 8:00 p.m.!

340
18:47.264 --> 18:49.032
-Hurry up and eat! -Okay.

341
18:50.434 --> 18:51.768
I got a lead!

342
18:51.835 --> 18:54.438
I was contacted about someone having seen Mr. Monden!

343
18:54.504 --> 18:57.407
A construction worker shared the photos in a group chat.

344
18:57.474 --> 19:00.978
A group chat with 170 people! Is that normal in Tokyo? Isn't that crazy?

345
19:01.578 --> 19:03.647
-I'll make room. -Hey!

346
19:03.714 --> 19:05.649
You're being a bit rough.

347
19:05.716 --> 19:07.050
Sorry.

348
19:09.853 --> 19:11.188
It's here.

349
19:11.255 --> 19:14.291
The traffic guide who stood here on the night of August 4th

350
19:14.358 --> 19:17.227
remembered stopping Mr. Monden's car.

351
19:17.294 --> 19:19.930
-There is construction ahead. -I have to turn around?

352
19:19.997 --> 19:21.665
-A car? -Yes, a car.

353
19:22.833 --> 19:27.371
To detour to Mr. Nikaido's condo, he needs to take this route.

354
19:27.437 --> 19:29.239
When the CCTV caught him, he was walking.

355
19:29.306 --> 19:30.207
Which means…

356
19:30.274 --> 19:32.042
He must have parked somewhere!

357
19:32.109 --> 19:34.745
If we know the plate number, we can trace the owner's contact.

358
19:34.811 --> 19:35.646
Car model?

359
19:35.712 --> 19:38.982
Unknown, but it's a white sedan. Do you have the camera footage there?

360
19:39.049 --> 19:40.884
More or less.

361
19:40.951 --> 19:43.287
Let's find this car! Bring it on!

362
19:43.353 --> 19:44.655
We're getting closer!

363
19:46.957 --> 19:49.960
Have something to drink and take a break.

364
19:51.128 --> 19:52.129
Okay.

365
19:54.665 --> 19:57.367
Did you figure out the meaning behind those 11 digits?

366
19:57.434 --> 19:59.236
Not at all.

367
19:59.303 --> 20:04.408
I think only Mr. Nikaido knows.

368
20:12.282 --> 20:13.216
Here.

369
20:13.984 --> 20:14.885
Thank you.

370
20:15.585 --> 20:20.023
So many things we don't know.

371
20:33.837 --> 20:34.938
Good morning.

372
20:39.142 --> 20:40.844
Should I move from here?

373
20:41.611 --> 20:42.879
Where is he?

374
20:44.181 --> 20:47.484
Mr. Nao went to collect security camera footage.

375
20:47.551 --> 20:49.619
We found a lead yesterday.

376
20:51.321 --> 20:52.723
Would you like some?

377
20:52.789 --> 20:54.758
Yes! Thank you.

378
20:57.728 --> 21:00.263
Did you walk around all day yesterday?

379
21:00.964 --> 21:02.599
Aren't you tired?

380
21:02.666 --> 21:04.267
I prefer moving around.

381
21:04.334 --> 21:07.437
It makes me feel like a police detective. I love it.

382
21:09.339 --> 21:11.108
Do you not get to do it often?

383
21:12.809 --> 21:15.579
My district has a small population.

384
21:15.645 --> 21:19.516
When a crime happens, oftentimes, I instantly know who did it.

385
21:19.583 --> 21:21.618
It's not even worth searching.

386
21:26.523 --> 21:29.726
You know him through work, right?

387
21:32.462 --> 21:36.533
Actually, I only met him last week.

388
21:40.570 --> 21:42.072
Do you trust him?

389
21:46.276 --> 21:51.615
Honestly, at first I thought, "What a nonchalant guy."

390
21:51.681 --> 21:53.316
I was the opposite.

391
21:54.384 --> 21:58.288
I met him in a night class at university.

392
21:59.356 --> 22:02.426
I worked at the same insurance company he's at now.

393
22:03.827 --> 22:06.062
Sorry, what are we talking about?

394
22:07.531 --> 22:09.266
You wanted to know how I met him, right?

395
22:09.332 --> 22:10.600
Yes! That's me.

396
22:10.667 --> 22:13.203
Sorry. Please continue.

397
22:15.238 --> 22:16.640
After work,

398
22:18.074 --> 22:23.213
he and I both studied risk management at university.

399
22:25.916 --> 22:29.953
He was knowledgeable, quick-witted, and confident.

400
22:30.020 --> 22:32.255
I thought he was trustworthy.

401
22:32.322 --> 22:35.125
I'm beginning to think so too.

402
22:36.092 --> 22:37.227
Am I wrong?

403
22:38.762 --> 22:40.030
Now,

404
22:41.598 --> 22:45.235
when I see his face, I think…

405
22:46.636 --> 22:49.840
"What a nonchalant guy."

406
22:51.241 --> 22:52.642
He's like that.

407
22:52.709 --> 22:54.811
He doesn't care which method he uses.

408
22:55.512 --> 22:59.583
But I feel like no matter what, he will find out the truth.

409
22:59.649 --> 23:00.851
So I trust him.

410
23:09.125 --> 23:10.260
Shall I help?

411
23:10.327 --> 23:11.828
With what?

412
23:11.895 --> 23:13.964
With what you're doing now.

413
23:14.030 --> 23:16.366
What?! Are you sure?

414
23:16.900 --> 23:20.136
But, don't you have work?

415
23:20.203 --> 23:23.540
I'm on summer vacation starting today. What should I look for?

416
23:24.808 --> 23:26.610
Then, thank you.

417
23:27.511 --> 23:29.446
I need your help to find a white car.

418
23:29.513 --> 23:30.347
Okay.

419
23:30.413 --> 23:31.481
It looks delicious!

420
23:35.619 --> 23:38.455
You aren't going anywhere for summer vacation?

421
23:39.456 --> 23:41.157
Everywhere is crowded.

422
23:42.125 --> 23:44.127
Too many people, yes.

423
23:44.194 --> 23:46.897
I want to go somewhere without people.

424
23:48.064 --> 23:49.366
Thank you for the food.

425
23:49.432 --> 23:51.568
I wonder what place isn't crowded these days.

426
23:53.904 --> 23:57.674
When my daughter was alive, we climbed mountains every year.

427
24:04.281 --> 24:06.917
Did he not tell you about our daughter?

428
24:08.785 --> 24:09.619
No.

429
24:15.091 --> 24:16.626
She died.

430
24:19.362 --> 24:20.697
She was six.

431
24:25.435 --> 24:28.905
That man just kept on blaming…

432
24:30.106 --> 24:31.274
himself.

433
24:39.049 --> 24:41.885
How is it going? Did you find the white sedan?

434
24:41.952 --> 24:44.588
It didn't appear in any parking lot.

435
24:44.654 --> 24:47.457
Is that even possible?

436
24:47.524 --> 24:49.392
Maybe they parked on the street?

437
24:49.459 --> 24:50.827
The search would never end.

438
24:51.461 --> 24:54.497
Maybe we should officially ask the police.

439
24:54.564 --> 24:56.499
Large-scale searches are their strength.

440
24:56.566 --> 24:58.735
I will find it tomorrow, no matter what!

441
25:01.538 --> 25:02.572
Hey, Ogoma.

442
25:03.206 --> 25:04.774
Can you come here now?

443
25:05.675 --> 25:08.211
I'm going to talk to Nono…

444
25:09.212 --> 25:10.880
about Ms. Tabatake.

445
25:10.947 --> 25:12.382
You should join me.

446
25:13.016 --> 25:13.917
Okay.

447
25:17.621 --> 25:19.689
Nono, can you hear us?

448
25:20.757 --> 25:24.461
Can I have this policeman listen in on us too?

449
25:26.129 --> 25:27.731
Hello.

450
25:27.797 --> 25:29.032
Hello.

451
25:29.099 --> 25:31.301
Look, this is the sky in Tokyo!

452
25:33.169 --> 25:37.007
Let's get to the point.

453
25:38.241 --> 25:42.512
Last time, there was something you couldn't say about your mom, right?

454
25:42.579 --> 25:44.014
Nono.

455
25:45.081 --> 25:48.985
Is it about what you mentioned to me at the hospital last time?

456
25:49.052 --> 25:50.353
Was my Mommy…

457
25:51.554 --> 25:53.289
killed?

458
25:59.863 --> 26:05.268
Can you tell us why you think that?

459
26:05.335 --> 26:06.870
Any reason is fine.

460
26:06.936 --> 26:09.639
We want to know what your Mom was thinking.

461
26:12.876 --> 26:13.943
Mommy…

462
26:15.011 --> 26:19.282
was always worried someone would come to our house.

463
26:20.250 --> 26:23.353
When there was a noise outside, she went to check right away.

464
26:23.420 --> 26:25.055
Did someone come?

465
26:26.322 --> 26:27.791
No, there was no one.

466
26:29.993 --> 26:31.094
-Is it this? -Yeah.

467
26:32.762 --> 26:34.497
Then, I'll make a star.

468
26:35.865 --> 26:39.669
She told me never to follow strangers, even if they spoke to me.

469
26:39.736 --> 26:41.504
She said it to me again and again.

470
26:41.571 --> 26:43.707
-You good? Okay. -I'm going!

471
26:46.976 --> 26:48.545
-I'm late! -Take care!

472
26:48.611 --> 26:49.679
Bye!

473
27:00.590 --> 27:02.792
What do you mean I can't turn back now?

474
27:06.629 --> 27:07.997
I'll call you back.

475
27:08.064 --> 27:10.433
Was she always like that?

476
27:10.500 --> 27:12.068
No.

477
27:12.135 --> 27:13.103
Welcome home.

478
27:13.169 --> 27:16.673
When did your Mom start acting scared?

479
27:16.740 --> 27:19.042
In the last few months, apparently.

480
27:19.109 --> 27:23.880
And a while before that, she told me she got a new job.

481
27:23.947 --> 27:26.382
Aside from being a mountain guide and a driver?

482
27:26.449 --> 27:27.283
Yes.

483
27:27.350 --> 27:29.753
I told her not to overwork,

484
27:30.553 --> 27:34.657
but she said this job doesn't take much time and pays well.

485
27:34.724 --> 27:38.561
Nono, did she ever tell you what the job was?

486
27:42.966 --> 27:45.235
I also don't know much.

487
27:47.704 --> 27:50.006
I'll look into that.

488
27:50.073 --> 27:51.174
Can you?

489
27:51.241 --> 27:54.244
Of course. Who do you think I am?

490
27:57.313 --> 27:58.815
-Chika. -Yes?

491
27:58.882 --> 28:01.417
May I ask a favor?

492
28:01.484 --> 28:02.452
Sure.

493
28:02.519 --> 28:04.020
Nono, don't worry.

494
28:04.654 --> 28:07.090
There's nothing to worry about.

495
28:07.157 --> 28:08.091
Okay.

496
28:10.126 --> 28:12.562
Huh? Tabatake's jobs?

497
28:13.196 --> 28:14.764
She was a guide and driver, right?

498
28:14.831 --> 28:16.966
Did she have another job?

499
28:17.033 --> 28:19.035
Part-time or short-term?

500
28:19.102 --> 28:20.370
How long is your vacation?

501
28:21.805 --> 28:23.239
Until tomorrow.

502
28:23.306 --> 28:24.641
Make sure you come back.

503
28:25.809 --> 28:27.343
Saruwatari is about to confess…

504
28:27.410 --> 28:29.979
She was interrogated for eight days straight.

505
28:30.046 --> 28:31.648
She's nearing her limit.

506
28:38.054 --> 28:40.690
I can ask the police to let you rest.

507
28:40.757 --> 28:44.460
No. If I refuse, I'll look more suspicious.

508
28:44.527 --> 28:46.863
It doesn't matter. It's just voluntary questioning.

509
28:48.298 --> 28:51.167
Please put your health first.

510
28:52.335 --> 28:53.303
Yes.

511
28:54.704 --> 28:56.506
Hello?

512
28:57.240 --> 28:59.108
How have you been?

513
29:00.143 --> 29:02.679
How are your injuries? How is the investigation going?

514
29:03.713 --> 29:07.383
I know it's their job, but the police sure are persistent, right?

515
29:10.887 --> 29:15.725
How can I make them believe what I say?

516
29:17.560 --> 29:18.695
The police

517
29:20.163 --> 29:23.499
are investigating under the assumption you're the culprit.

518
29:24.000 --> 29:26.803
They haven't arrested you for questioning yet, right?

519
29:26.870 --> 29:28.671
Arrested?

520
29:29.873 --> 29:33.576
If you say anything that sounds even slightly like admitting guilt,

521
29:33.643 --> 29:35.211
they'll switch to it.

522
29:36.479 --> 29:38.448
Even though I did nothing?

523
29:38.514 --> 29:41.818
Ogoma is working hard every day for you.

524
29:41.885 --> 29:43.152
Don't forget that.

525
29:48.191 --> 29:50.526
Can you tell Ogoma something for me?

526
29:52.161 --> 29:56.232
That as long as I have even one ally, I can bear it.

527
30:00.136 --> 30:01.537
I'll tell him.

528
30:02.639 --> 30:05.375
We're always here to talk, both me and Ogoma.

529
30:08.778 --> 30:10.446
Thank you.

530
30:12.882 --> 30:14.717
-Are you going somewhere? -Yes.

531
30:14.784 --> 30:18.488
I'm going to check the parking lots around Mr. Nikaido's condo again.

532
30:18.554 --> 30:19.722
Hold on. I got it.

533
30:19.789 --> 30:21.257
-Hold on. -But why?

534
30:21.324 --> 30:23.760
-I have to go! I have no time! -It's okay. Come on.

535
30:24.661 --> 30:26.029
Just stay here for now.

536
30:26.095 --> 30:27.196
I have no time.

537
30:27.263 --> 30:29.232
Leave going outside until tomorrow.

538
30:30.667 --> 30:33.169
Is Harune really in Tokyo?

539
30:33.236 --> 30:35.004
She definitely took a plane bound for Haneda.

540
30:35.571 --> 30:39.242
My sister, Harune, left her medicine at home.

541
30:39.309 --> 30:40.143
Yes?

542
30:40.209 --> 30:43.079
But she's on airplane mode, so I can't reach her.

543
30:43.146 --> 30:44.047
Okay.

544
30:44.113 --> 30:45.315
Without it,

545
30:46.549 --> 30:47.583
she'll die!

546
30:47.650 --> 30:50.586
You keep making up the most outrageous lies.

547
30:50.653 --> 30:53.289
-Police do it often. -I've never done it.

548
30:53.356 --> 30:54.624
Nor will you?

549
30:54.691 --> 30:56.592
As a rule, I don't want to.

550
30:56.659 --> 30:58.528
Flexibility is important these days.

551
30:58.594 --> 31:00.797
-You're just saying whatever. -Ogoma.

552
31:01.531 --> 31:03.199
Have you contacted Ms. Aya?

553
31:03.800 --> 31:05.234
-I haven't. -Why? Do it!

554
31:05.301 --> 31:08.404
I'll get evidence, then come back to Hokkaido and call her.

555
31:08.471 --> 31:09.572
So let me go.

556
31:09.639 --> 31:13.576
By the way, isn't this bed too small?

557
31:15.244 --> 31:17.313
It's fine.

558
31:17.380 --> 31:19.415
It's definitely too small!

559
31:21.050 --> 31:27.156
Akane is a capable person, but sometimes she misses things like this.

560
31:28.424 --> 31:30.526
This is definitely too small. Let me--

561
31:31.194 --> 31:32.595
-What? -This room…

562
31:33.529 --> 31:35.431
This is your daughter's room, right?

563
31:42.939 --> 31:44.640
Did she like stars?

564
31:50.013 --> 31:50.980
Yes.

565
31:55.051 --> 31:56.986
Did Akane tell you something?

566
31:58.454 --> 32:00.490
Yes, a little.

567
32:00.556 --> 32:01.591
What did she say?

568
32:02.525 --> 32:04.360
That it was a traffic accident.

569
32:05.395 --> 32:06.763
That's about it.

570
32:12.001 --> 32:13.870
It was right after she entered elementary school.

571
32:16.506 --> 32:17.640
Dad!

572
32:18.841 --> 32:25.048
I had that day off, so I went to her school to see her.

573
32:29.252 --> 32:31.621
You must think I'm an overprotective parent.

574
32:31.687 --> 32:32.588
No.

575
32:33.423 --> 32:36.659
She was in nursery school up until then,

576
32:36.726 --> 32:39.729
and either Akane or I still had to pick her up,

577
32:39.796 --> 32:41.397
so I was just worried.

578
33:15.031 --> 33:17.200
I called an ambulance right away.

579
33:18.134 --> 33:21.070
But she didn't make it.

580
33:22.472 --> 33:23.973
Hey, turn her over here.

581
33:27.510 --> 33:29.579
-Decide! -Which one do you want to stick up?

582
33:29.645 --> 33:32.115
This one? Oh, this one?

583
33:32.181 --> 33:33.749
Okay, here you go.

584
33:43.860 --> 33:47.930
You probably feel the same.

585
33:50.099 --> 33:56.305
Why is it so hard to part with someone who is no longer in this world?

586
33:58.441 --> 34:01.444
They're always…

587
34:02.011 --> 34:04.147
on your mind, right?

588
34:07.917 --> 34:09.085
Thank you.

589
34:09.652 --> 34:10.520
Hot!

590
34:11.420 --> 34:12.622
Yes.

591
34:13.389 --> 34:14.891
It's strange, isn't it?

592
34:17.560 --> 34:19.896
Wait!

593
34:24.066 --> 34:24.901
There!

594
34:24.967 --> 34:28.204
-Whoa! -Nice! Stick them on harder!

595
34:49.258 --> 34:51.160
Was there a parking lot over here?

596
34:51.227 --> 34:53.462
Your residential map is old.

597
34:53.529 --> 34:55.932
This place became an empty lot and then a parking lot.

598
34:56.766 --> 34:58.434
You did great finding it.

599
34:58.501 --> 35:01.103
All that walking around paid off.

600
35:01.837 --> 35:02.738
This is the place.

601
35:02.805 --> 35:05.141
-Nice. -What do you mean "nice"?

602
35:06.943 --> 35:08.044
Thank you.

603
35:09.212 --> 35:10.246
Welcome.

604
35:11.247 --> 35:12.281
You again.

605
35:12.348 --> 35:13.583
Hello.

606
35:13.649 --> 35:16.185
I would like to ask about the night of August 4th.

607
35:16.252 --> 35:18.588
I'm busy. Ask someone else.

608
35:18.654 --> 35:20.423
Please! Can you listen to me?

609
35:20.489 --> 35:22.758
-The "car accident" was a lie, right? -It was, sorry.

610
35:23.693 --> 35:25.795
You were lying too.

611
35:25.861 --> 35:28.698
I showed many people those photos.

612
35:28.764 --> 35:33.669
Most took a long look at them, and tried to jog their memory.

613
35:33.736 --> 35:36.606
But only you said, "I haven't seen them," right away.

614
35:36.672 --> 35:38.908
I haven't seen either of them.

615
35:39.642 --> 35:42.345
I'm Ogoma, with Hokkaido Police.

616
35:42.411 --> 35:45.848
I'm Nao from Zennichi Insurance Research.

617
35:47.083 --> 35:48.117
Take care.

618
35:49.385 --> 35:52.955
On the night of August 4th, this man talked to me.

619
35:53.022 --> 35:55.157
He said he was looking for this woman.

620
35:55.224 --> 35:56.826
Looking for her?

621
35:58.060 --> 36:01.364
What about that car parked in the lot behind?

622
36:01.430 --> 36:02.565
It's mine.

623
36:03.132 --> 36:08.271
August 4th at 9:00 p.m.

624
36:08.971 --> 36:13.276
He gave me 10,000 yen and asked me not to tell anyone.

625
36:15.444 --> 36:17.213
-Quite visible. -Yes.

626
36:17.280 --> 36:19.048
-Can you stop it here? -Yes.

627
36:19.115 --> 36:20.416
I can see the plate numbers!

628
36:20.483 --> 36:21.817
Yes! Thank you so much!

629
36:21.884 --> 36:23.219
I love you!

630
36:23.286 --> 36:24.453
Come on!

631
36:24.520 --> 36:26.989
-Do you have his contact information? -You do, right?

632
36:27.056 --> 36:27.990
Yes!

633
36:28.057 --> 36:29.792
All right!

634
36:29.859 --> 36:32.495
-Who are you calling? -070… Huh? This number.

635
36:32.561 --> 36:33.629
Why are you calling?

636
36:33.696 --> 36:36.198
-I'll call him over. Oh, come on! -No!

637
36:36.265 --> 36:39.035
You need more information first. Are you stupid?

638
36:39.101 --> 36:40.569
A plate check?

639
36:40.636 --> 36:43.773
Yes, here's the plate number. Shinagawa 301…

640
36:43.839 --> 36:45.308
What are you doing?

641
36:45.941 --> 36:47.243
Nothing.

642
36:47.310 --> 36:49.679
Don't tell me you're sneakily investigating?

643
36:49.745 --> 36:51.414
I am not…

644
36:51.480 --> 36:53.616
Why do you sound so unsure?

645
36:53.683 --> 36:57.086
I told you, we're officers! Just follow the higher-ups!

646
36:58.220 --> 36:59.622
Here.

647
36:59.689 --> 37:00.589
Wait a moment.

648
37:00.656 --> 37:02.158
An officer from Hokkaido?

649
37:02.224 --> 37:03.859
He's investigating something.

650
37:06.329 --> 37:09.198
I'm Tamura from Yoyogi Central Police Station.

651
37:09.765 --> 37:12.535
A person from your station is here.

652
37:13.069 --> 37:14.070
Yes.

653
37:14.136 --> 37:15.838
I told you not to act on your own!

654
37:17.139 --> 37:18.074
Sorry.

655
37:18.140 --> 37:19.809
When you come back, report everything.

656
37:20.509 --> 37:21.711
Don't come empty-handed.

657
37:22.445 --> 37:23.746
Did something happen?

658
37:23.813 --> 37:25.014
No, nothing.

659
37:26.215 --> 37:27.316
Hello, sir!

660
37:27.383 --> 37:28.217
Good work today.

661
37:28.284 --> 37:29.218
Thank you.

662
37:29.285 --> 37:30.753
Shirokuma Car Lease?

663
37:30.820 --> 37:32.955
Shall I ask the lease company?

664
37:34.590 --> 37:37.426
No. Call Mr. Monden.

665
37:41.263 --> 37:42.198
Hello.

666
37:42.732 --> 37:46.469
Um… Hello? I am…

667
37:47.837 --> 37:50.039
I'm sorry to bother you.

668
37:50.106 --> 37:53.242
I'm Suzuki from Shirokuma Car Lease.

669
37:53.309 --> 37:57.413
We have an urgent notice about the vehicle you're using.

670
37:58.414 --> 37:59.315
What?

671
37:59.382 --> 38:02.284
We found parts in it that need replacing.

672
38:02.351 --> 38:03.552
So for your safety,

673
38:03.619 --> 38:06.989
we must ask you to swap to a substitute vehicle right away.

674
38:07.056 --> 38:08.057
Today?

675
38:08.124 --> 38:11.794
Yes. I'm really sorry to bother you! When would you be available?

676
38:17.967 --> 38:19.835
Will Mr. Monden really come?

677
38:19.902 --> 38:22.204
I don't know.

678
38:30.780 --> 38:33.783
I have something to tell you.

679
38:34.450 --> 38:39.021
Chika gave me some documents on Ms. Tabatake's household finances.

680
38:40.623 --> 38:43.759
Bank accounts, credit card statements, and so on.

681
38:44.693 --> 38:48.264
Wages for the guide and driver jobs are deposited there.

682
38:48.330 --> 38:53.035
But no deposits for the other job Nono mentioned.

683
38:53.602 --> 38:56.439
So it's paid in cash?

684
38:56.505 --> 38:58.741
Do you know how much Nono's treatment costs?

685
38:59.742 --> 39:01.677
I can't tell from the bank account.

686
39:01.744 --> 39:04.246
But look at this.

687
39:04.313 --> 39:06.549
We can roughly see Nono's medical costs.

688
39:07.216 --> 39:07.883
What?

689
39:07.950 --> 39:10.820
Nono's illness is covered by insurance, right?

690
39:10.886 --> 39:13.322
It shouldn't cost this much. This is astronomical.

691
39:14.290 --> 39:17.760
Maybe she was prescribed drugs not covered by insurance.

692
39:18.427 --> 39:21.797
It's roughly one million yen per month.

693
39:21.864 --> 39:24.600
The math doesn't add up.

694
39:25.501 --> 39:28.971
Even working as a guide and driver, she cannot cover all of that.

695
39:30.739 --> 39:34.176
A super well-paying job that pays solely in cash…

696
39:34.243 --> 39:36.812
As a police officer, I can only think of one thing.

697
39:38.247 --> 39:39.682
Crime.

698
39:40.516 --> 39:43.586
If even I can figure it out, the police must have a clue, right?

699
39:43.652 --> 39:44.887
They didn't tell you?

700
39:44.954 --> 39:48.524
They never told me. That's why I'm here.

701
39:48.591 --> 39:50.593
Will Nono be okay?

702
39:50.659 --> 39:53.729
If she can't afford those medical costs anymore…

703
39:53.796 --> 39:57.700
I won't let that happen. I will make sure she is okay.

704
40:06.575 --> 40:07.610
Why are you grinning?

705
40:07.676 --> 40:09.578
Shirokuma Car Lease!

706
40:09.645 --> 40:11.780
Sorry for the trouble.

707
40:16.085 --> 40:17.186
Hey!

708
40:18.320 --> 40:19.655
-Wait! -Hey!

709
40:19.722 --> 40:20.656
Wait!

710
40:20.723 --> 40:21.991
Why are you running?

711
40:22.057 --> 40:23.659
-Hey! -Hold on!

712
40:23.726 --> 40:25.694
Why are you running?!

713
40:25.761 --> 40:27.530
Stop!

714
40:29.732 --> 40:31.433
Monden!

715
40:32.468 --> 40:34.370
Ogoma!

716
40:43.479 --> 40:45.180
Which way?

717
40:45.247 --> 40:46.382
This way!

718
40:47.583 --> 40:50.085
This way, I guess.

719
40:50.152 --> 40:51.387
Wait!

720
40:54.290 --> 40:55.558
Wait!

721
40:56.592 --> 40:57.960
Stop right there!

722
40:58.027 --> 41:00.796
EMERGENCY EXIT

723
41:03.065 --> 41:04.300
Not that way.

724
41:05.134 --> 41:05.968
Hey!

725
41:06.035 --> 41:08.837
I'm telling you! Stop!

726
41:08.904 --> 41:11.240
Where?

727
41:14.410 --> 41:17.046
Got him! Ogoma, I got him!

728
41:17.112 --> 41:18.614
It hurts!

729
41:18.681 --> 41:19.949
Wait!

730
41:30.492 --> 41:32.027
Okay, okay!

731
41:32.561 --> 41:34.697
I give up!

732
41:35.230 --> 41:36.899
Get your dirty hands off him!

733
41:39.068 --> 41:39.935
Sorry!

734
41:40.002 --> 41:42.237
-What're you doing?! -Bring it on!

735
41:45.374 --> 41:46.141
It hurts!

736
41:48.577 --> 41:50.913
Here we go again! Stop!

737
41:55.818 --> 41:57.486
What? Who are you?

738
41:57.553 --> 41:59.154
As if I'd tell you, idiot.

739
42:04.994 --> 42:06.595
Just give up already!

740
42:18.340 --> 42:21.577
Amateur! If you don't hold back, I'll die!

741
42:21.644 --> 42:22.911
You're the idiot here!

742
42:29.785 --> 42:32.554
I know who you are. Got it?

743
42:39.962 --> 42:42.064
You're Ryutaro Monden, right?

744
42:43.699 --> 42:45.134
I bet you want to know who I am.

745
42:50.639 --> 42:51.807
Follow me.

746
43:04.319 --> 43:06.622
Don't tell anyone what I'm about to tell you.

747
43:06.689 --> 43:08.057
I'll think about it.

748
43:08.123 --> 43:09.525
Don't be cocky.

749
43:41.523 --> 43:43.859
Can you tell me your story?

750
43:47.062 --> 43:48.864
The security camera footage with me on it…

751
43:53.268 --> 43:54.603
Who in the police…

752
43:55.437 --> 43:56.739
has seen it?

753
43:58.907 --> 44:01.176
I don't know what happened on that mountain…

754
44:01.243 --> 44:02.978
How will you take responsibility?

755
44:03.045 --> 44:04.847
We have to admit it failed.

756
44:04.913 --> 44:07.416
Can you keep this a secret?

757
44:08.083 --> 44:09.051
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
